    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Add a draft template package as a template segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --resource TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Template package resource. Use local:///<abs_path> for a local\r\n                              zip or template://<template_id> for a template material resource.\r\n          --title TEXT        Template segment title. Falls back to the template resource id.\r\n          --start <duration>  Target start time; explicit unit required (us, ms, s, min).\r\n          --track-index INT:INT in [-1 - 2147483647] [-1]  \r\n                              Video track index for inserting the template segment; -1 lets the\r\n                              draft layer choose a compatible track.\r\n          --scene TEXT:{default,commerce,group,enterprise,personal,0,1,3,4,10} \r\n                              Template scene tag: default|commerce|group|enterprise|personal\r\n                              (also accepts raw 0/1/3/4/10).\r\n          --duration <duration> \r\n                              Override the template duration; explicit unit required (us, ms,\r\n                              s, min).\r\n          --muted TEXT        Mute the template segment audio (true/false).\r\n          --is-ae TEXT        Treat the package as an AE template (true/false).\r\n          --new-track         Insert the template into a newly created target track.\r\n          --category-id TEXT  Template category id metadata.\r\n          --category-name TEXT \r\n                              Template category name metadata.\r\n          --resource-dir TEXT Download directory for a template:// resource package.\r\n          --material-options-json TEXT \r\n                              Template material download options as a JSON object or @path\r\n          --slot-overrides TEXT \r\n                              Pre-fill template slots with a JSON array, each item\r\n                              `{source_slot_id, kind:text|media, content|resource}`.\r\n          --slot-overrides-hex TEXT \r\n                              Same as --slot-overrides but hex-encoded to avoid shell escaping.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Add a downloaded local template zip to the draft\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template add --ref local://demo --resource local:///tmp/templates/<id>.zip\r\n  # Add a template directly by its platform template resource id\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template add --ref local://demo --resource template://<template_id>\r\n  # Add with an explicit title, start time, track and category metadata\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template add --ref local://demo --resource template://<id> \\\r\n      --title \"Intro\" --start 1s --track-index 0 --scene commerce --category-id 123\r\n  # Add to a new track, muted, and pre-fill a media slot\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template add --ref local://demo --resource template://<id> \\\r\n      --new-track --muted true \\\r\n      --slot-overrides '[{\"source_slot_id\":\"<id>\",\"kind\":\"media\",\"resource\":\"local:///abs/clip.mp4\"}]'\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Add a draft template package as a template segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --resource TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Template package resource. Use local:///<abs_path> for a local\r\n                              zip or template://<template_id> for a template material resource.\r\n          --title TEXT        Template segment title. Falls back to the template resource id.\r\n          --start <duration>  Target start time; explicit unit required (us, ms, s, min).\r\n          --track-index INT:INT in [-1 - 2147483647] [-1]  \r\n                              Video track index for inserting the template segment; -1 lets the\r\n                              draft layer choose a compatible track.\r\n          --scene TEXT:{default,commerce,group,enterprise,personal,0,1,3,4,10} \r\n                              Template scene tag: default|commerce|group|enterprise|personal\r\n                              (also accepts raw 0/1/3/4/10).\r\n          --duration <duration> \r\n                              Override the template duration; explicit unit required (us, ms,\r\n                              s, min).\r\n          --muted TEXT        Mute the template segment audio (true/false).\r\n          --is-ae TEXT        Treat the package as an AE template (true/false).\r\n          --new-track         Insert the template into a newly created target track.\r\n          --category-id TEXT  Template category id metadata.\r\n          --category-name TEXT \r\n                              Template category name metadata.\r\n          --resource-dir TEXT Download directory for a template:// resource package.\r\n          --material-options-json TEXT \r\n                              Template material download options as a JSON object or @path\r\n          --slot-overrides TEXT \r\n                              Pre-fill template slots with a JSON array, each item\r\n                              `{source_slot_id, kind:text|media, content|resource}`.\r\n          --slot-overrides-hex TEXT \r\n                              Same as --slot-overrides but hex-encoded to avoid shell escaping.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Add a downloaded local template zip to the draft\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template add --ref local://demo --resource local:///tmp/templates/<id>.zip\r\n  # Add a template directly by its platform template resource id\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template add --ref local://demo --resource template://<template_id>\r\n  # Add with an explicit title, start time, track and category metadata\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template add --ref local://demo --resource template://<id> \\\r\n      --title \"Intro\" --start 1s --track-index 0 --scene commerce --category-id 123\r\n  # Add to a new track, muted, and pre-fill a media slot\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template add --ref local://demo --resource template://<id> \\\r\n      --new-track --muted true \\\r\n      --slot-overrides '[{\"source_slot_id\":\"<id>\",\"kind\":\"media\",\"resource\":\"local:///abs/clip.mp4\"}]'\r\n",
